      "cooked": "<p>fixed using this</p><aside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"122716\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/ncp/48/66573_2.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/solved-column-width-in-form-designer/122716/2?utm_source=chatgpt.com\">[SOLVED] Column width in form designer</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/erpnext/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #BF1E2E; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">ERPNext</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    That for, you have to apply the client script for that doctype. \nPlease check it. \nfrappe.ui.form.on('Test DocType', {\n    refresh: function(frm) {\n        var $form_layout = frm.fields_dict['section_break_tbtz'].wrapper;\n        var $columns = $form_layout.find('.form-column');\n        if ($columns.length === 2) {\n            $($columns[0]).css({\n                'max-width': '70%',\n                'flex': '0 0 70%'\n            });\n            $($columns[1]).css({\n                'max-width': '3…\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n",
